steps.body:
The lesson on passing and forwarding used a **parameter pack** inside `emplace_back`: `typename... Args` is any number of types, and `std::forward<Args>(args)...` forwards each argument. A pack can do much more than forward:

```cpp
template <typename... Ts>
void count_fields(const Ts&... fields) {
    std::cout << sizeof...(fields) << " fields\n";
}

count_fields("AAPL", 19275, 100);  // 3 fields
```

- `sizeof...(fields)` is the number of elements, a compile-time constant, so `static_assert(sizeof...(fields) > 0, "...")` can demand at least one.
- An **expansion** repeats a pattern once per element, separated by commas. The pattern is the expression just left of the `...`: `f(fields...)` calls `f(a, b, c)`, and `f(g(fields)...)` calls `f(g(a), g(b), g(c))`.
- You can't index a pack or loop over it, but it expands inside braces too, so `const std::int64_t values[] = {xs...};` copies it into an array you can loop over.

To visit the elements one at a time, peel off the first and recurse on the rest. `if constexpr` from the templates lesson ends the recursion when nothing is left:

```cpp
template <typename First, typename... Rest>
void print_fields(const First& first, const Rest&... rest) {
    std::cout << first;
    if constexpr (sizeof...(rest) > 0) {
        std::cout << ',';
        print_fields(rest...);  // one argument fewer
    }
}

print_fields("AAPL", 19275, 100);  // AAPL,19275,100
std::cout << '\n';
```

Each call is a separate instantiation with one argument fewer, and at `-O2` the chain inlines away. For `print_fields(a, b, c)` with an `int`, a `long`, and a `double`, g++ emits five calls into the stream's own output functions in a row, and no call to `print_fields` at all.

example.code:
#include <cstdint>
#include <iostream>

template <typename... Ts>
void count_fields(const Ts&... fields) {
    std::cout << "fields: " << sizeof...(fields) << '\n';
}

template <typename First, typename... Rest>
void print_fields(const First& first, const Rest&... rest) {
    std::cout << first;
    if constexpr (sizeof...(rest) > 0) {
        std::cout << ',';
        print_fields(rest...);
    } else {
        std::cout << '\n';
    }
}

std::int64_t to_cents(std::int64_t dollars) {
    return dollars * 100;
}

template <typename... Ts>
void print_cents(const Ts&... dollars) {
    print_fields(to_cents(dollars)...);  // print_fields(to_cents(a), to_cents(b), ...)
}

template <typename... Ts>
std::int64_t widest(const Ts&... spreads) {
    static_assert(sizeof...(spreads) > 0, "widest needs at least one spread");
    const std::int64_t values[] = {spreads...};  // the pack, copied into an array
    std::int64_t best = values[0];
    for (std::int64_t v : values) {
        if (v > best) {
            best = v;
        }
    }
    return best;
}

int main() {
    count_fields();
    count_fields("AAPL");
    count_fields("AAPL", 19275, 100);
    print_fields("AAPL", 19275, 100);
    print_fields("MSFT", 'B', 41010, 50, 0.25);
    print_cents(192, 41, 139);
    std::cout << "widest: " << widest(10, 5, 25, 1) << '\n';
    return 0;
}

